   187	    - There are 2-3 source components, each formed by one colored dense rectangle containing grey marker pixels plus one same-color adjacent 2-pixel domino outside the rectangle.
   188	    - There is exactly one plain yellow rectangle with no grey marker pixels; it is the target and is at least as tall and wide as every source rectangle.
   189	
   190	    Rule:
   191	    - Identify the yellow target rectangle and crop it as the output canvas, initially filled with yellow.
   192	    - For each source component, detect the domino orientation after separating the dense rectangle from the external domino.
   193	    - A horizontal domino means row migration: preserve each grey pixel's top/bottom edge-relative row and map its column proportionally into the target width; a vertical domino means column migration: preserve its left/right edge-relative column and map its row proportionally into the target height.
   194	    - Draw all column-migration grey pixels first, then all row-migration grey pixels, on the yellow crop.
